{"availability":"available","full":"Wyzer-Lang/wyzer","name":"wyzer","description":"The Wyzer Programming Language","category":"Other","language":"OCaml","stars":250,"forks":9,"created":"2025-04-13T06:49:38Z","updated":"2026-10-01T16:42:29Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://wyzer-lang.vercel.app/","topics":["compiler","language","wyzer"],"demo":"https://wyzer-lang.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:35:17.314Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T22:35:17.314Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T22:35:17.314Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T22:35:17.314Z","stars":250,"forks":9}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Wyzer is a statically typed, compiled, resource-oriented programming language with integrated distributed safety via choreographic programming and a perceus memory model.","\"Simplicity is not the absence of power. It is power without pretense.\" Atiksh Sharma","In traditional distributed programming, you write separate code for the client and the server, and hope their communication protocols match up. Choreographic programming allows you to write a single, unified view of the entire distributed system. The compiler then mathematically projects this single script into deadlock-free, independent binaries for each physical node (e.g., Client and Server)."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Wyzer-Lang/wyzer/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"c28bb2df7c1bd7b476bd20c79ff4b0b0a14df2ed1a4de5e223990c0bfe4eafc6","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T22:35:17.430Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:35:17.430Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Wyzer is a statically typed, compiled, resource-oriented programming language with integrated distributed safety via choreographic programming and a perceus memory model.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Wyzer-Lang/wyzer/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"c28bb2df7c1bd7b476bd20c7